Before you open this pull request, check:

- [ ] Each commit has `Signed-off-by:` with your real name
      (https://openwrt.org/submitting-patches).
- [ ] The description says what you tested and on which hardware.
      "Not tested on hardware" is a valid answer; say it.
- [ ] No proprietary files: no stock firmware, no vendor source code
      without a GPL-compatible licence, no dumps of ART / tp_data.
- [ ] Code taken from another project names the author and the source.
- [ ] If an AI tool wrote part of the change, the commit has an
      `Assisted-by:` trailer.

See CONTRIBUTING.md.
